# The shape of a personal denylist. Copy it to the path that
#   node tools/runtime-paths.mjs public-scan-denylist
# prints (or set AGENTDESK_PUBLIC_SCAN_DENYLIST), then replace these made-up values with your own.
# Never commit the real one: it is a list of exactly what you are keeping private.
#
# Format: <id> /<regex>/<flags>   flags from imsuv; the scanner adds g itself.
# Ids are lowercase words joined by hyphens, unique across this file and secret-rules.txt.
# A rule that can match an empty string is refused, since it would match everywhere.

# Your name in every form it takes in code: paths, bundle ids, prose. A lookahead keeps a public
# handle that starts with it allowed.
owner-name /jane(?!doe-public)/i
owner-email /jane\.doe@example\.com/i

# Infrastructure that identifies you: a tailnet name, a domain, account ids.
tailnet /example-tailnet\.ts\.net/i
owner-domain /\bjane-doe\.example\b/i
cloud-account /0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef/
